The big addition over UT2003 is Onslaught, the new vehicle mode where teams link up power nodes across a big outdoor map. Assault is back from the original game, and all the UT2003 maps come along for the ride.', 'A few of us played the demo all last week and the netcode feels a lot better than 2003 did at launch. We will have a proper review up once we have spent some time with the full game.

If you want to set up a game, post in the Forums and we will get some people together.', 812, 1, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 0);

Far Cry is the one to watch if you just bought a new video card. The jungle levels look incredible and the draw distance is something else. Condition Zero comes with the Deleted Scenes single player campaign and an updated multiplayer game with bots.', 'Early word from the forums is that Far Cry wants at least a Radeon 9600 or a GeForce FX 5700 to look decent, and that the CZ bots are surprisingly good.

Steam users can buy Condition Zero online if you do not feel like driving to the store.', 1046, 1, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 1);

The 24 port switch gave out at about 2am on Saturday, so we ran the rest of the night on two smaller hubs and a lot of patience. FragMaster99 took the CS tournament again, and NoScope came in a close second.', 'Thanks to everyone who brought extra power strips and to Hexen_Dave for the pizza run. Photos are up in the LAN Parties forum.

The April LAN is already being planned, sign up in the forum if you want a seat.', 638, 4, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 0);

Valve has said very little since the source code leak last October. Vivendi''s last financial report still lists the game for this year, which is about all anyone has on the record.', 'The good news is that Valve has been showing the game to the press again, and the people who have played it say it is coming along. The bad news is that we have heard that before.

Our guess: not before summer. Feel free to tell us we are wrong in the comments.', 1493, 1, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 1);

If you signed up on the official site and have not heard anything, you are in good company. The beta thread in our Online and MMO forum is already past 40 replies.', 'Blizzard has not said anything about a release date beyond "when it''s done", which surprised nobody.

We will keep the beta thread open for anyone who wants to compare notes on the sign-up process.', 977, 5, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 0);

The lighting model is the part that is hard to describe to someone who has not seen it. Every light casts real-time shadows, and the UAC corridors we walked through felt unsettling because the darkness is doing the work, not scripted jump scares.', 'Framerate on the demo rig held up reasonably well, though the machine running it was clearly built for the occasion and not representative of what most of our readers have under their desks. A staffer on hand would only say the engine "scales", which could mean anything.

We also got a brief look at a few monster models, including a revenant-like enemy that the crowd seemed to enjoy more than the id rep standing next to it.

No release date was confirmed beyond the usual "when it''s done", though several outlets are reporting a possible summer window. We will believe it when there is a box on the shelf at EB. In the meantime, if you want to argue about it, the thread is open in our Forums.', 2187, 2, 0, 0, 'admin', 0, 'R', 2);
